                "text": "In March, the House overwhelmingly passed the Pandemic Unemployment Fraud Enforcement Act to extend the statute of limitations to prosecute criminals who stole billions in COVID-era unemployment insurance benefits.\n\n@USDOL Inspector General\u2019s Office has ID'd a number of investigations involving millions of tax dollars that have been or will be jeopardized in the future if the Senate fails to act on this bill.\n\nEvery day the Senate delays is another day criminals are getting away with the greatest theft of tax dollars in U.S. history.",
