                "reply_count": 7,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today, alongside @RepDavid, I sent a letter to Network for Hope, a Kentucky-based tax-exempt Organ Procurement Organization, demanding documents and records related to allegations of improper Medicare billing, financial conflicts of interest, and unsafe practices.\n\nOrgan procurement organizations play a critical role in saving lives and enjoy the generous status of being tax-exempt. But that mission collapses the moment they put profit ahead of patient safety. The American people deserve full transparency, and the Ways and Means Committee will ensure every organization that has engaged in these practices is held accountable.",
